{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfRD2FM6Thh5zgRE2vAgb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The tanh fit works best, with an rms of 0.015 that's essentially at the noise floor, converging on a fraction of about 0.385, consistent with the nonparametric estimate of 0.38-0.39. Though I'm now second-guessing whether the simulator's length term is being modeled correctly.\n\nFor the tanh estimate, I want to refine it using averaged proxy values across seeds - proxy_ship averaging around 1.8509 and mean_len around 617.0 - then compute the fraction as L/(Q+L) using the fitted model at that length. I'm settling on approximately 0.385 as my estimate given the expected tolerance is a few hundredths.\n\nMoving to the next question, in the true world the diff between ppo and bon is 0.27, favoring ppo, but I recognize this diff could vary across other consistent worlds with different gold divergence rates. My plan is two gold runs at gold_n=5500 with a cutoff of ±0.1, and I'll set bon's n to 270 to match the same KL level. For the next part, I need to work out the KL value at 2160 steps using the fitted exponential formula, then solve for n from there.\n\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1542,"cache_read_input_tokens":50063,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1542,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21bfc462-9181-41d6-8cf8-2278d57b5046","uuid":"1500c0eb-0c35-4410-b1ae-76a7f08cfe5c","timestamp":"2026-09-26T01:47:33.814Z"}
