{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfRD55jEmCSSz1Nr1BS1a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. `/app/answers.json` is written and valid, with about 3750 of the 9000 GPU-hour budget spent.\n\n**What the lab showed**\n\n- **KL laws are exact and closed-form.** Best-of-n sits at `log(n) − (n−1)/n` nats, not `log(n)`. PPO approaches its target as `kl·(1 − exp(−steps/τ))` with τ ≈ 1009 steps, independent of the target. The proposed 945-step run therefore reaches KL 4.60, not the 7.57 the notes assumed.\n- **The length term is real and saturating.** Sweeping `len_pen` at fixed KL moves proxy reward along one shared concave curve of mean length. A tanh fit lands at the measurement noise floor. At the proposed recipe's length of about 617 tokens the length term is 0.72 of a 1.85 proxy reward.\n- **Gold win rates diverge by method at equal KL.** With 1000 human comparisons each, PPO-945 won 0.81 and best-of-270 won 0.54 at the same KL. The length-penalised best-of-717 won 0.94, while the low-KL options scored near 0.03.\n\n**Answers**\n\n| Question | Answer | Basis |\n|---|---|---|\n| q1 | n = 270 | Solve the bon KL law for 4.602 nats |\n| q2 | 0.388 | Length term over measured proxy reward |\n| q3 | Two gold runs, 5500 comparisons each, cut at ±0.1 on the win-rate difference | Uses the full 4400 budget; difference noise is about 0.01 |\n| q4 | `bon_b` | 0.94 gold win rate versus 0.81 for the next best |\n| q5 | n = 2163 | Full 2160-step run reaches KL 6.68 |\n\n**Caveat on the notebook.** The notes' claim that best-of-n needs n = 1940 to match the recipe rests on the wrong KL formula and on the unreached target KL. The notes' claim that extra length is \"quality\" is contradicted by the length-penalised best-of-n winning the human comparison decisively."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":867,"cache_read_input_tokens"